From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sysdm: the Virtual Memory dialog of Windows 11.

Advanced system settings, Performance, Advanced, Change: "Automatically
manage paging file size for all drives" on top, which writes
"?:\pagefile.sys" to PagingFiles as Windows does; Custom size, System managed
size and No paging file under it; the total on the Advanced page. The value
may be missing or a REG_SZ and an entry is found wherever it is in the list.
Only the system's drive is listed: the host keeps the paging file there
(host/init/arctic-init.c), and removes one that is no longer wanted itself.
What is chosen counts without Set too. The words are Windows' in English,
Ukrainian and Russian.
